---
/* Several families of one surname, drawn as rivers.

   Each lane is one family this archive follows: the dots along it are places it
   can put a document in, and the fan at the right is where that family ended
   up. Beneath the lanes go the households of the name that are real and
   documented and NOT yet on any lane, so the picture cannot quietly imply that
   everything has been placed.

   Promoted out of Defranceschi, where it was the best drawing in the estate and
   the only archive that had it. It took no props at all — 15.6KB of one
   family's branches were written into the component itself — which is why the
   one other archive that wanted something like it wrote a second, different
   component of the same name rather than use this one.

   The data is one prop now and the arithmetic stays here:

     rivers  { lanes, unplaced, loose }

   lanes     [{ key, colour, label, href, read, conf, nodes, ends }]
             nodes are the places along the lane, ends the fan at its right
   unplaced  households of the name that are documented and not yet placed
   loose     the labels under the rule at the foot
   unplacedHead / looseHead / looseNote
             the headings over the two holding pens and the italic note at the
             end of the second. All three are the archive's words. The pens are
             drawn ONLY when they hold something: an empty heading is a claim
             the archive has looked and found nothing, and nobody has said so.
             looseNote has no default (it used to print "the commonest
             patronymic in Italy" under every archive's pen, which is true of
             one surname in one country).
   unplacedAfter
             a lane key. The unplaced block is drawn under THAT lane rather
             than under every lane, and everything below it moves down to
             make room. Omit it and the block stays at the foot.
   bridges   [{from, to, conf, label, href}] — A CANDIDATE JOIN BETWEEN TWO
             LANES, or between a lane and an unplaced household, on evidence
             short of a document. `from` and `to` are lane keys, and `to` may
             instead name an entry in `unplaced`.

   Any archive that can say which families it follows, where each began and
   where each went, gets the drawing. What it must not do is invent a lane to
   fill the picture: an empty band is a true statement, a guessed one is not.

   WHAT A LANE AND A PEN CARRY (2nd round, 25 October 2026; every field is optional and data written for the older
   component draws as it did). Defranceschi's page was the best of the eight archives' because it said, for every lane,
   how far its evidence reaches and, for every pen, what was in it and why; the other archives drew the same figure
   and said neither. The full contract is kit/docs/lines.md and the words are made in kit/lib/lines.js.

     lane   status      documented | inferred | origin-unknown | family-lore, drawn as a small mark and a line of
                        small capitals under the lane title («Documented 1628–1791 · origin inferred Carnian»);
                        `conf`, the old free string, is drawn only when a lane has no status
            statusNote  the words after the tier;  span  [first, last] documented year;  members  people slugs
     node   { place, year, why, person, evidence } or the old [place, year, why]. `person` makes the dot link to the
            person, not to the top of a page; `evidence` (read | indexed | scanned | tree | inferred | disputed |
            none) draws a node that is not read from a document hollow and dashed, like a soft ending
     pens   [{ id, kind, head, note, items, members, count }]  kind is not-yet-placed or different-stock. A pen's
            heading carries a count derived from the data («8 households · 31 people»), its `note` is printed
            under it, and its members are listed, each linked to a person page, beneath the drawing. The old
            `unplaced` / `loose` still work and become two pens; `unplacedNote` is new.
     props  personBase (default /people/), names ({slug: name}) for the member lists

   Nothing here decides a status or a count for an archive: tools/checklines.py holds the data to its own claims.

   A BRIDGE IS THE HONEST THIRD STATE BETWEEN THOSE TWO. Asked for by the
   Defranceschi session, which had a real one to draw: Kobler's letter puts a
   Giovanni Battista De Franceschi in Fiume from the County of Pazin «intorno
   al 1740», and a Joannes Baptista de Franceschi baptises at Fiume in 1748
   whose son heads the Rijeka chain. That is a candidate join between a lane
   and an unplaced household, and it is inferred, not documented. Without a
   bridge the only ways to say it were to promote it to a lane, which would be
   a guess drawn as a fact, or to leave it out, which is not what the archive
   knows.

   So it is drawn to lose an argument with everything around it: dotted, in
   neutral ink rather than either lane's colour, thinner and fainter than any
   lane, with its reason written small. It reads as a question. */
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
/* An SVG <title> is the graphic's accessible name and its tooltip, so whatever
   goes in is READ ALOUD and shown on hover. These take their text straight
   from the data, which is written in the archives' light markup — so a rich
   «why» was being announced to a screen reader as "star CORRECTED 8 Oct 2026.
   asterisk asterisk 1931 is the year he DIED…" with its brackets and hrefs
   intact. plain() is in the next file along and exists for exactly this. */
import { plain } from "../lib/md.js";
import { statusLine, TIER_WORD, node as normNode, evidenceOf, personPath, slugName, member as normMember,
         pensOf, penCount, wrap, clip, lanePeople, ledger, KIND_WORD } from "../lib/lines.js";

/* THE CAPTION IS THE ARCHIVE'S, NOT THE KIT'S.
   This component was promoted out of Defranceschi and its caption came with
   it - the teal river, Argentina, Monheim, Brazil and Ticino - so every other
   archive that adopted the drawing got Defranceschi's words underneath it,
   describing rivers it does not have. Raised by that session, whose words they
   are. It is a prop now with NO default (an archive that passes none draws no
   caption), and Defranceschi passes its own. */
/* THE SVG TITLE IS THE GRAPHIC'S ACCESSIBLE NAME, AND IT CARRIED A COUNT.
   «Six families of one surname, and the road each of them took» was hardcoded
   here, so it was what a screen reader announced for the whole drawing — and
   it went on announcing six after Defranceschi drew its seventh lane, because
   a number written into a component cannot follow the data it describes. An
   archive that renames its lanes has no way to correct it, and nobody sees an
   accessible name in a page diff. It is a prop now, defaulting to the string
   that was hardcoded so no adopting archive changes. */
import "../styles/ours.css";
import { directMap, OURS_LEGEND } from "../lib/directline.js";
/* directLine: the archive's src/data/direct-line.json. A NODE of a person in it is filled with the tint (`is-ours`,
   data-ours); a LANE the archive marks `ours: true` has a tinted band under its colour (data-ours="lane:<key>"). Nothing is
   tinted without the file (kit/docs/family-ribbon.md). */
const { rivers, caption, title, personBase = "/people/", names = {}, directLine = null } = Astro.props;
const DM = directMap(directLine);
const nodeOurs = (nd) => !!(nd.person && DM.has(String(nd.person).replace(/^\/people\//, "").replace(/\/+$/, "")));
const LANES = rivers?.lanes ?? [];
/* TWO FIGURES ON ONE PAGE MUST NOT SHARE AN ID. riversttl and riverread were fixed strings, so a page with two drawings
   pointed both SVGs at the first title and let the first figure's panel answer the second's clicks (found by Luwinski's
   18 Oct 2026 corrections). The id is derived from the lanes, so it is distinct per drawing and the same on every build. */
const uid = (() => { let h = 0; for (const c of LANES.map((l) => l.key + "|" + l.label).join("~")) h = (h * 31 + c.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0; return h.toString(36); })();
const BRIDGES = rivers?.bridges ?? [];

const W = 1040;
const BH = 140, BGAP = 152;
/* THE PENS, LAID OUT BELOW THE RULE. They are drawn only when they hold something (an empty heading is a claim the
   archive has looked and found nothing). Each pen is a heading (20 below its top), its households in rows of three
   (the first row 40 below the top, 26 between rows), then its note, wrapped, 15 a line. The next pen starts 20 below
   the last thing in this one, and the block ends 24 below the last thing of all. With the two old lists and no notes
   these come to exactly the numbers they always were: second heading at +80, its row at +100, the block 124 tall,
   each extra row of households 26 more. */
const PENS = pensOf(rivers);
const HAS_PENS = PENS.length > 0;
const COLX = (i) => 110 + (i % 3) * 310;
const NOTE_CHARS = 150, NOTE_LH = 15;
let cursor = 0;
const PL = PENS.map((p) => {
  const t = cursor;
  const rows = Math.ceil(p.items.length / 3);
  const itemsY0 = t + 40;
  let last = p.items.length ? itemsY0 + (rows - 1) * 26 : t + 20;
  const noteLines = p.note ? wrap(p.note, NOTE_CHARS) : [];
  const noteY0 = last + (p.items.length ? 26 : 22);
  if (noteLines.length) last = noteY0 + (noteLines.length - 1) * NOTE_LH;
  cursor = last + 20;
  return { ...p, t, rows, itemsY0, noteLines, noteY0, last };
});
const END = HAS_PENS ? PL[PL.length - 1].last + 24 : 0;
const BLOCK = HAS_PENS ? 22 + END : 0;
const LED = ledger(rivers);

/* WHERE THE BLOCK SITS IN THE STACK, AND WHY IT IS NO LONGER ALWAYS LAST.
   It began at the foot, because "everything not yet placed" belongs after
   everything that is. But the lanes are ordered by the archive, and the first
   of them is usually the line that archive descends from — so the reader who
   has just finished it is at the exact moment the unplaced households are
   worth showing, and instead has five more families to scroll past before
   meeting them. Naming a lane in `unplacedAfter` puts the block directly
   under that lane and moves the rest of the stack down to make room. Naming
   nothing, or naming a lane that is not drawn, leaves it at the foot exactly
   where it was, so no archive that does not ask for this sees any change. */
let CUT = LANES.length;
if (rivers?.unplacedAfter && HAS_PENS) {
  const ci = LANES.findIndex((l) => l.key === rivers.unplacedAfter);
  if (ci > -1) CUT = ci + 1;
}
/* The 36 is not padding for its own sake: it is the one empty row a bridge
   label can use when the block is in the middle of the stack. See GAPS. */
const INSET = CUT < LANES.length ? BLOCK + 36 : 0;
const BANDS = LANES.map((_, i) => {
  const y0 = 34 + i * BGAP + (i >= CUT ? INSET : 0);
  return { y0, sp: y0 + 76, h: BH };
});
const LOOSE_Y = 34 + CUT * BGAP + 22;   // rule
const VH = 34 + LANES.length * BGAP + INSET + (CUT < LANES.length ? 20 : BLOCK);
const X0 = 150, X1 = 700, XE = 902;

/* Where a bridge may attach. A lane is anchored at the head of its own spine,
   because a speculative join between two families is nearly always a claim
   about where they START; an unplaced household is anchored on its own dot
   below the rule, which is exactly where it sits until somebody places it. */
const anchor = (key) => {
  const li = LANES.findIndex((l) => l.key === key);
  if (li > -1) return { x: X0, y: BANDS[li].sp, lane: true };
  for (const p of PL) {
    if (p.kind !== "not-yet-placed") continue;
    const ui = p.items.findIndex((l) => l.name === key);
    if (ui > -1) return { x: COLX(ui), y: LOOSE_Y + p.itemsY0 + Math.floor(ui / 3) * 26, lane: false };
  }
  return null;
};
/* A bridge naming something that is not on the drawing is dropped rather than
   drawn to nowhere, and the count is reported in the figure's caption so the
   omission is visible instead of silent. */
/* WHERE A BRIDGE LABEL CAN GO WITHOUT LANDING ON SOMETHING.
   The first version anchored it at the bow and it ran off the left edge. The
   second clamped it and it ran straight across the node row instead - measured
   on the Defranceschi page at x=92 y=551, over Svetvincenat, Pula, Fazana and
   Premantura, all of which sit at y=535 on the lane below. The gutter left of
   the first node is 58px wide, so no label of useful length fits there and
   this was never about wordiness.

   The bands are 140 tall on a 152 pitch, so between every pair of them is a
   12px strip with nothing in it at any x. The label goes in the strip nearest
   the curve's midpoint, and runs rightward across a row that is empty by
   construction. Below the last band there are no strips and no node rows
   either, so the midpoint is used as it is.

   ⚠ AND NO STRIP MAY TAKE TWO LABELS. Nearest-strip is a function of the
   curve, not of the drawing, so two bridges whose midpoints fall either side
   of the same strip were both sent to it and printed on top of each other —
   two sentences superimposed into a line of nonsense, which is worse than
   either being absent. Measured on the Defranceschi page the moment the
   unplaced block moved up the stack: the Kobler join and the Sanvincenti
   godparent join both landed at y=180. So a strip is CLAIMED when a label
   takes it, and the next label falls to the nearest strip still free. A
   label one band away from its curve can still be followed — the curve is
   dotted and the eye follows it — and a label nobody can read cannot. */
const GAPS = BANDS.map((b) => b.y0 + BH + 6);
/* When the unplaced block is in the middle of the stack it opens one more
   empty row, 20px under its last line and 14px above the band that follows —
   which is what the 36 in INSET buys. It must be UNDER that line and not
   beside it: the block's own labels run right across the drawing at three
   fixed x positions, so a strip level with them is not empty at the x a
   bridge label starts from. Measured: a label put 12px higher ran straight
   through «Ticino» and «Michigan». */
if (CUT < LANES.length) GAPS.push(LOOSE_Y + END);
GAPS.sort((a, b) => a - b);
const TAKEN = new Set();
const labelY = (y) => {
  if (!GAPS.length || y > GAPS[GAPS.length - 1] + BGAP) return y;
  const free = GAPS.filter((g) => !TAKEN.has(g));
  if (!free.length) return y;
  const g = free.reduce((best, c) => (Math.abs(c - y) < Math.abs(best - y) ? c : best), free[0]);
  TAKEN.add(g);
  return g;
};
const BR = BRIDGES.map((b) => ({ ...b, a: anchor(b.from), b: anchor(b.to) }))
                  .filter((x) => x.a && x.b);
const BR_LOST = BRIDGES.length - BR.length;

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ words and links, made once */
const peopleWord = (n) => `${n} ${n === 1 ? "person" : "people"}`;
const pHref = (person) => u(personPath(person, personBase));
const nameOf = (m) => m.name || names[m.person] || slugName(m.person);
const TIER_N = LED.tiers;
const DESC = [
  `${LED.lanes} ${LED.lanes === 1 ? "line" : "lines"}`
    + (LED.lanes - LED.unstated > 0
        ? " (" + ["documented", "inferred", "origin-unknown", "family-lore"].filter((k) => TIER_N[k]).map((k) => `${TIER_N[k]} ${TIER_WORD[k]}`).join(", ") + ")"
        : ""),
  ...PL.map((p) => `${penCount(p)} ${KIND_WORD[p.kind]}`),
  BR.length ? `${BR.length} candidate ${BR.length === 1 ? "join" : "joins"}, on evidence short of a document` : "",
].filter(Boolean).join("; ") + ".";
/* every lane, ready to draw: its words, its people and its nodes in the one shape */
const LV = LANES.map((lane) => {
  const st = statusLine(lane);
  const ppl = lanePeople(lane);
  const nodes = (lane.nodes ?? []).map((n) => { const o = normNode(n); return { ...o, ev: evidenceOf(o.evidence) }; });
  const ends = (lane.ends ?? []).map((n) => { const o = normNode(n, "end"); return { ...o, ev: evidenceOf(o.evidence) }; });
  return { lane, st, ppl, nodes, ends, members: (lane.members ?? []).map(normMember) };
});
const WITH_MEMBERS = PL.filter((p) => p.members.length > 0);
const LANE_MEMBERS = LV.filter((v) => v.members.length > 0);
---
<figure class="rivers" data-lanes={LED.lanes} data-households={LED.households} data-other-stock={LED.otherStock}>
  <a class="rivers-skip" href={`#rr-end-${uid}`}>Skip the drawing</a>
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 1040 ${VH}`} role="group" aria-labelledby={`rt-${uid}`} aria-describedby={`rd-${uid}`}>
    <title id={`rt-${uid}`}>{title ?? `The lines of this name: ${LANES.length} ${LANES.length === 1 ? "lane" : "lanes"}, and the road each of them took`}</title>
    <desc id={`rd-${uid}`}>{DESC}</desc>
    {LV.map(({ lane, st, ppl, nodes, ends }, li) => {
      const b = BANDS[li];
      const n = nodes.length;
      const step = n > 2 ? (X1 - X0) / (n - 1) : (X1 - X0) / 2;
      const lineEnd = X0 + step * (n - 1);
      const spread = Math.min(b.h / 2 - 18, 16 + ends.length * 13);
      const spineEnd = Math.max(lineEnd, X1);
      const lore = st.tier === "family-lore";
      return (
        <g role="group" data-lane-key={lane.key} data-status={st.tier ?? ""} class={lane.ours && directLine ? "is-ours-lane" : undefined} data-ours={lane.ours && directLine ? `lane:${lane.key}` : undefined}
           aria-label={`${lane.label}. ${st.text}. ${n} ${n === 1 ? "place" : "places"}, ${ends.length} ${ends.length === 1 ? "destination" : "destinations"}${ppl.length ? ", " + peopleWord(ppl.length) : ""}.`}>
          {lane.ours && directLine && <rect class="lane-ours" x="0" y={b.y0} width={W} height={b.h} rx="10" />}
          <rect x="0" y={b.y0} width={W} height={b.h} rx="10"
                fill={lane.colour} opacity={lane.parallel ? 0.04 : 0.055}
                stroke={lane.parallel ? lane.colour : "none"}
                stroke-dasharray={lane.parallel ? "5 5" : ""} stroke-opacity="0.4" />
          <text x="12" y={b.y0 + 21} class="lane-label" fill={lane.colour}>{lane.label}</text>
          {st.tier && (
            <g class="tier" aria-hidden="true">
              {st.tier === "documented" && <circle cx="17" cy={b.y0 + 33.5} r="4.2" fill={lane.colour} />}
              {st.tier === "inferred" && <>
                <circle cx="17" cy={b.y0 + 33.5} r="4.2" fill="none" stroke={lane.colour} stroke-width="1.4" />
                <path d={`M 17 ${b.y0 + 29.3} A 4.2 4.2 0 0 1 17 ${b.y0 + 37.7} Z`} fill={lane.colour} />
              </>}
              {st.tier === "origin-unknown" && <circle cx="17" cy={b.y0 + 33.5} r="4.2" fill="none" stroke={lane.colour} stroke-width="1.4" />}
              {st.tier === "family-lore" && <circle cx="17" cy={b.y0 + 33.5} r="4.2" fill="none" stroke={lane.colour} stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="1.6 1.8" />}
            </g>
          )}
          <text x={st.tier ? 28 : 12} y={b.y0 + 37} class="lane-conf" data-status-line>{st.text}</text>
          {ppl.length > 0 && <text x="12" y={b.y0 + b.h - 26} class="lane-people">{peopleWord(ppl.length)} on this line</text>}
          <a href={u(lane.href)} class="lane-link"><text x="12" y={b.y0 + b.h - 9} class="lane-read" fill={lane.colour}>{lane.read}</text></a>

          <line x1={X0} y1={b.sp} x2={spineEnd} y2={b.sp} stroke={lane.colour}
                stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.34"
                stroke-dasharray={lane.parallel || lore ? "12 7" : ""} />
          {st.tier === "inferred" && (
            <line class="lead-in" x1={X0 - 64} y1={b.sp} x2={X0 - 12} y2={b.sp} stroke={lane.colour}
                  stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.4" stroke-dasharray="1 7" />
          )}
          {st.tier === "origin-unknown" && (
            <g class="lead-in">
              <line x1={X0 - 56} y1={b.sp} x2={X0 - 12} y2={b.sp} stroke={lane.colour}
                    stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.4" stroke-dasharray="6 6" />
              <circle cx={X0 - 60} cy={b.sp} r="3.2" fill="none" stroke={lane.colour} stroke-width="1.4" opacity="0.5" />
            </g>
          )}

          {ends.map((nd, ei) => {
            const y = ends.length === 1 ? b.sp
              : b.sp - spread + (ei * (spread * 2) / (ends.length - 1));
            const soft = nd.place.endsWith("?") || (nd.ev && nd.ev.soft);
            const e = nd.place.replace("?", "");
            const href = nd.person ? pHref(nd.person) : u(nd.href || lane.href);
            return (
              <g class="node end" tabindex="0" role="button"
                 aria-label={`${e}${nd.place.endsWith("?") ? ", not verified" : ""}${nd.ev ? ", " + nd.ev.label : ""}. ${nd.person ? "Opens the person's page." : "Opens the page that tells it."}`}
                 data-place={e} data-year={soft ? "unverified" : ""}
                 data-why={plain(nd.why)} data-lane={lane.label} data-ev={nd.ev ? nd.ev.label : ""}
                 data-href={href} data-read={nd.person ? "Open the person's page" : `Read the ${e} story`}>
                <title>{e} — {plain(nd.why)}{nd.ev ? ` [${nd.ev.label}]` : ""}</title>
                <path d={`M ${spineEnd} ${b.sp} C ${X1 + 90} ${b.sp}, ${XE - 90} ${y}, ${XE} ${y}`}
                      fill="none" stroke={lane.colour} stroke-width="1.6" opacity="0.5"
                      stroke-dasharray={soft ? "3 4" : ""} />
                <circle cx={XE} cy={y} r="6.5" fill="transparent" />
                <circle cx={XE} cy={y} r="3.4" fill={lane.colour}
                        fill-opacity={soft ? 0.35 : 1} />
                <text x={XE + 9} y={y + 4} class={soft ? "endlab soft" : "endlab"}>{e}</text>
                <circle class="ring" cx={XE} cy={y} r="11" />
              </g>
            );
          })}

          {nodes.map((nd, i) => {
            const x = X0 + i * step;
            const soft = !!(nd.ev && nd.ev.soft);
            const href = nd.person ? pHref(nd.person) : u(lane.href);
            const yTxt = nd.year;
            return (
              <g class={(soft ? "node soft" : "node") + (nodeOurs(nd) ? " is-ours" : "")} data-ours={nodeOurs(nd) ? String(nd.person).replace(/^\/people\//, "").replace(/\/+$/, "") : undefined} tabindex="0" role="button"
                 aria-label={`${nd.place}${nd.year && nd.year !== "—" ? ", " + nd.year : ""}${nd.ev ? ", " + nd.ev.label : ""}. ${nd.person ? "Opens the person's page." : "Opens the page that tells this line."}`}
                 data-place={nd.place} data-year={nd.year} data-why={plain(nd.why)} data-lane={lane.label}
                 data-ev={nd.ev ? nd.ev.label : ""} data-person={nd.person ?? ""}
                 data-href={href} data-read={nd.person ? "Open the person's page" : (lane.read ?? "").replace(" →","")}>
                <title>{nd.place}{nd.year && nd.year !== "—" ? ` · ${nd.year}` : ""} — {plain(nd.why)}{nd.ev ? ` [${nd.ev.label}]` : ""}</title>
                <circle cx={x} cy={b.sp} r="8.5" fill="var(--panel)" stroke={lane.colour} stroke-width="2.6"
                        stroke-dasharray={soft ? "3.4 2.6" : ""} />
                <circle cx={x} cy={b.sp} r="3" fill={lane.colour} fill-opacity={soft ? 0.3 : 1} />
                <text x={x} y={b.sp - 19} class="place">{nd.place}</text>
                <text x={x} y={b.sp + 27} class="year" fill={lane.colour}>{yTxt}</text>
                <circle class="ring" cx={x} cy={b.sp} r="14" />
              </g>
            );
          })}
        </g>
      );
    })}
    {BR.map((br) => {
      const a = br.a, z = br.b;
      /* Bowed out to the left of the lane heads, so the curve is read as
         something added across the picture rather than as part of either
         lane's own line. */
      const bow = a.lane && z.lane ? Math.min(78, 34 + Math.abs(z.y - a.y) / 4) : 46;
      const mx = (a.x + z.x) / 2 - bow, my = (a.y + z.y) / 2;
      const dash = br.conf === "lore" ? "2 6" : "3 5";
      return (
        <g class="bridge node" tabindex="0" role="button"
           aria-label={`A candidate join, on evidence short of a document${br.label ? ": " + plain(br.label) : ""}`}
           data-place={br.label || "A candidate join"}
           data-year={br.conf === "lore" ? "testimony" : "inferred"}
           data-why={br.label ? plain(br.label) : null} data-lane="A candidate join, not a document"
           data-href={br.href ? u(br.href) : ""} data-read="Where this join is argued">
          <title>{br.label ? plain(br.label) + " — " : ""}a candidate join, on evidence short of a document</title>
          <path d={`M ${a.x} ${a.y} C ${a.x - bow} ${a.y}, ${z.x - bow} ${z.y}, ${z.x} ${z.y}`}
                fill="none" stroke="var(--ink-2)" stroke-width="1.2"
                stroke-dasharray={dash} opacity={br.conf === "lore" ? 0.34 : 0.48} />
          <circle cx={a.x} cy={a.y} r="2.6" fill="var(--ink-2)" opacity="0.5" />
          <circle cx={z.x} cy={z.y} r="2.6" fill="var(--ink-2)" opacity="0.5" />
          {br.label && (
            <text x={Math.max(8, mx + 8)} y={labelY(my) + 3} class="bridge-label">{plain(br.label)}</text>
          )}
        </g>
      );
    })}
    {HAS_PENS && (
    <g>
      <line x1="12" y1={LOOSE_Y} x2={W - 12} y2={LOOSE_Y} stroke="var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 4" />
      {PL.map((p) => {
        const other = p.kind === "different-stock";
        return (
        <g class="pen" data-kind={p.kind} data-count={p.items.length} role="group" aria-label={`${plain(p.head)}. ${penCount(p)}.`}>
          <text x="12" y={LOOSE_Y + p.t + 20} class="loose-head">{plain(p.head)}<tspan class="pen-count" dx="10">· {penCount(p)}</tspan></text>
          {p.items.map((it, i) => {
            const cx = COLX(i), cy = LOOSE_Y + p.itemsY0 + Math.floor(i / 3) * 26;
            const href = it.person && !it.href ? pHref(it.person) : u(it.href);
            return (
            <g class="node" tabindex="0" role="button"
               aria-label={`${it.name}, ${KIND_WORD[p.kind]}. Opens where it is written up.`}
               data-place={it.name} data-year={other ? "—" : "unplaced"} data-why={plain(it.why)}
               data-lane={other ? "Attached to no line here" : "Not yet placed on a line"} data-href={href}
               data-read={`Where ${it.name} is written up`}>
              <title>{it.name} — {plain(it.why)}</title>
              <circle cx={cx} cy={cy} r="7" fill="transparent" />
              <circle cx={cx} cy={cy} r="4.5" fill="none" stroke={other ? "var(--ink-3)" : "var(--ink-2)"}
                      stroke-width={other ? 1.6 : 1.8} stroke-dasharray={other ? "2 2" : ""} />
              <text x={cx + 12} y={cy + 4} class="loose">{clip(it.name, 38)}</text>
              <circle class="ring" cx={cx} cy={cy} r="12" />
            </g>
            );
          })}
          {p.noteLines.length > 0 && (
            <text x="12" y={LOOSE_Y + p.noteY0} class="loose-note" data-pen-note={p.id}>
              {p.noteLines.map((ln, k) => <tspan x="12" dy={k ? NOTE_LH : 0}>{ln}</tspan>)}
            </text>
          )}
        </g>
        );
      })}
    </g>
    )}
  </svg>
  {/* THE PHONE READS A LIST, NOT A SHRUNK DRAWING. At 390px the drawing was 660px wide in a sideways scroll with labels near
      7px. Under 700px the drawing is hidden and this list, the same lanes in the same order with the same links, is shown.
      It says what the drawing says: the status of every lane, the people counted on it, the count in every pen and the
      note under it. */}
  <div class="rivers-list">
    {LV.map(({ lane, st, ppl, nodes, ends }) => (
      <section class="rl-lane" style={`--lc:${lane.colour}`} data-status={st.tier ?? ""}>
        <h3>{lane.label}</h3>
        <p class="rl-conf">{st.tier && <span class="rl-tier" aria-hidden="true" data-tier={st.tier}></span>}{st.text}</p>
        {ppl.length > 0 && <p class="rl-people">{peopleWord(ppl.length)} on this line</p>}
        <ol class="rl-nodes">{nodes.map((nd) => (
          <li>{nd.person ? <a href={pHref(nd.person)}><b>{nd.place}</b></a> : <b>{nd.place}</b>}{nd.year && nd.year !== "—" ? <span> · {nd.year}</span> : null}{nd.ev && nd.ev.soft ? <i class="rl-ev"> ({nd.ev.label})</i> : null}</li>
        ))}</ol>
        {ends.length > 0 && <p class="rl-ends"><span>Went on to</span> {ends.map((e) => e.place.replace("?", "")).join(" · ")}</p>}
        <a class="rl-read" href={u(lane.href)}>{lane.read}</a>
      </section>
    ))}
    {BR.length > 0 && <section class="rl-pen"><h3>Candidate joins, not documents</h3>
      <ul>{BR.map((br) => <li>{br.label ? plain(br.label) : "A candidate join"}{br.href ? <> · <a href={u(br.href)}>where it is argued</a></> : null}</li>)}</ul></section>}
    {PL.map((p) => (
      <section class="rl-pen" data-kind={p.kind} aria-labelledby={`pn-${uid}-${p.id}`}>
        <h3 id={`pn-${uid}-${p.id}`}>{plain(p.head)} <span class="rl-count">· {penCount(p)}</span></h3>
        {p.items.length > 0 && <ul>{p.items.map((l) => <li><a href={l.person && !l.href ? pHref(l.person) : u(l.href)}>{l.name}</a></li>)}</ul>}
        {p.note && <p class="rl-note">{plain(p.note)}</p>}
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="riverread" id={`rr-${uid}`} aria-live="polite">
    <b>Click or tab any dot</b> — the stops tell you what the document behind them says, and the destinations on the right tell their own story and link to it. Click a second time to go there.
  </div>
  {caption && <figcaption set:html={caption} />}
  {directLine && (LV.some(({ lane, nodes }) => (lane.ours) || nodes.some(nodeOurs))) && <p class="ours-leg"><span class="ours-sw"></span>{OURS_LEGEND}</p>}
  {(WITH_MEMBERS.length > 0 || LANE_MEMBERS.length > 0) && (
    <div class="rivers-members" data-members>
      {LANE_MEMBERS.map(({ lane, members }) => (
        <details class="rm" data-lane-key={lane.key}>
          <summary>{lane.label} — {peopleWord(members.length)} on this line</summary>
          <ul>{members.map((m) => <li><a href={pHref(m.person)}>{nameOf(m)}</a>{m.reason ? <span class="rm-why"> — {plain(m.reason)}</span> : null}</li>)}</ul>
        </details>
      ))}
      {WITH_MEMBERS.map((p) => (
        <details class="rm" data-pen={p.id}>
          <summary>{plain(p.head)} — {peopleWord(p.members.length)}</summary>
          <ul>{p.members.map((m) => <li><a href={pHref(m.person)}>{nameOf(m)}</a>{m.reason ? <span class="rm-why"> — {plain(m.reason)}</span> : null}</li>)}</ul>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  )}
  {BR_LOST > 0 && (
    <p class="rivers-note">{BR_LOST === 1
      ? "One candidate join names a lane or household that is not on this drawing, and is not drawn."
      : BR_LOST + " candidate joins name a lane or household that is not on this drawing, and are not drawn."}</p>
  )}
  <span class="rivers-end" id={`rr-end-${uid}`} tabindex="-1"></span>
</figure>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    /* scoped to ITS OWN figure: the script sits right after it, so two drawings on a page do not share a panel */
    var fig = document.currentScript && document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;
    if (!fig) return;
    var host = fig.querySelector(".riverread");
    if (!host) return;
    var rest = host.innerHTML;
    function show(g) {
      var place = g.getAttribute("data-place"), year = g.getAttribute("data-year"),
          why = g.getAttribute("data-why"), lane = g.getAttribute("data-lane");
      var href = g.getAttribute("data-href"), read = g.getAttribute("data-read");
      var ev = g.getAttribute("data-ev");
      host.innerHTML = '<span class="rr-lane"></span><b class="rr-place"></b>'
        + '<span class="rr-year"></span><span class="rr-why"></span>'
        + (ev ? '<span class="rr-ev"></span>' : '')
        + (href ? '<a class="rr-go" href="' + href + '"></a>' : '');
      if (ev) host.querySelector(".rr-ev").textContent = "Rests on: " + ev;
      host.querySelector(".rr-lane").textContent = lane;
      host.querySelector(".rr-place").textContent = place;
      host.querySelector(".rr-year").textContent = year && year !== "\u2014" ? year : "";
      host.querySelector(".rr-why").textContent = why;
      if (href) host.querySelector(".rr-go").textContent = (read || "Read on") + " \u2192";
      fig.querySelectorAll(".node").forEach(function (n) { n.classList.remove("sel"); });
      g.classList.add("sel");
    }
    fig.querySelectorAll(".node").forEach(function (g) {
      g.addEventListener("click", function () {
        var was = g.classList.contains("sel"), href = g.getAttribute("data-href");
        show(g);
        if (was && href) window.location.href = href;
      });
      g.addEventListener("mouseenter", function () { show(g); });
      g.addEventListener("focus", function () { show(g); });
      /* Focus has already shown the dot (above), so Enter or Space is the second step: go there. A keyboard reader
         used to be able to show a dot and never follow it. */
      g.addEventListener("keydown", function (e) {
        if (e.key === "Enter" || e.key === " ") {
          e.preventDefault();
          var href = g.getAttribute("data-href");
          if (g.classList.contains("sel") && href) window.location.href = href; else show(g);
        }
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .rivers{margin:0}
  .rivers svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;overflow:visible}
  .lane-label{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:13px;font-weight:600}
  .lane-conf{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;
    text-transform:uppercase;fill:var(--ink-3)}
  .lane-read{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;text-anchor:start}
  .lane-link{text-decoration:none}
  .lane-link:hover .lane-read{text-decoration:underline}
  .place{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;fill:var(--ink);
    text-anchor:middle;paint-order:stroke;stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:3.4px}
  .year{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;text-anchor:middle;
    paint-order:stroke;stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:3px}
  .endlab{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:11.5px;fill:var(--ink-2)}
  .endlab.soft{fill:var(--ink-3);font-style:italic}
  .loose-head{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;
    text-transform:uppercase;fill:var(--ink-3)}
  .loose{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12.5px;fill:var(--ink-2)}
  .loose-note{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12px;font-style:italic;fill:var(--ink-3)}
  .pen-count{fill:var(--ink-2);font-weight:600}
  .lane-people{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;fill:var(--ink-3)}
  .rivers .node.soft .place{font-style:italic}
  .rivers .node{cursor:help}
  .rivers .node:hover circle:first-of-type,
  .rivers .node:focus circle:first-of-type{r:11}
  .rivers .node:focus{outline:none}
  .rivers .node:focus .place{fill:var(--accent)}
  /* a real, visible focus ring for the keyboard (the radius change above is not enough on its own) */
  .rivers .node .ring{fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2;opacity:0;pointer-events:none}
  .rivers .node:focus-visible .ring{opacity:1}
  .rivers .node:focus-visible .loose,.rivers .node:focus-visible .endlab{fill:var(--ink);text-decoration:underline}
  .rivers .lane-link:focus-visible .lane-read{text-decoration:underline;outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}
  .rivers-skip{position:absolute;left:-9999px;top:auto;font:600 13px var(--sans);padding:6px 10px;background:var(--panel);
    color:var(--accent);border:1px solid var(--accent);border-radius:6px;z-index:5}
  .rivers-skip:focus{left:0;top:-34px}
  .rivers{position:relative}
  .rivers-end{display:block;height:0;outline:none}
  .rivers .node.sel circle:first-of-type{r:11;stroke-width:3.4}
  .riverread{margin-top:18px;padding:14px 18px;border-left:3px solid var(--accent);
    background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;font-family:var(--sans);
    font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--ink-2);min-height:52px}
  .riverread .rr-lane{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;
    letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);margin-bottom:4px}
  .riverread .rr-place{color:var(--ink);font-size:16px}
  .riverread .rr-year{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--accent);margin-left:9px}
  .riverread .rr-why{display:block;margin-top:5px}
  .riverread .rr-ev{display:block;margin-top:6px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.08em;
    text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}
  .riverread .rr-go{display:inline-block;margin-top:8px;font-weight:600;
    font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none}
  .riverread .rr-go:hover{text-decoration:underline}
  .rivers .node.end{cursor:pointer}
  .rivers .node.end:hover .endlab,
  .rivers .node.end:focus .endlab{fill:var(--ink);text-decoration:underline}
  .rivers .node.end.sel .endlab{fill:var(--ink);font-weight:600}
  /* A bridge has to lose an argument with everything around it. */
  .rivers-note{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-3);margin-top:8px}
  .rivers .bridge-label{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:10.5px;fill:var(--ink-3);
    font-style:italic;letter-spacing:.01em}
  .rivers .bridge{cursor:pointer}
  .rivers .bridge:hover path,.rivers .bridge:focus path{opacity:.8}
  .rivers figcaption{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);
    margin-top:14px;max-width:78ch;line-height:1.6}
  .rivers-list{display:none}
  .rl-lane{border-left:4px solid var(--lc,var(--accent));padding:2px 0 2px 14px;margin:0 0 18px}
  .rl-lane h3,.rl-pen h3{margin:0 0 2px;font:600 15px/1.3 var(--sans)}
  .rl-conf{margin:0 0 6px;font:11px/1.3 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}
  .rl-nodes{margin:0 0 6px;padding:0;list-style:none;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px 14px;font:14px/1.5 var(--sans);color:var(--ink)}
  .rl-nodes span{color:var(--ink-3);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px}
  .rl-ends{margin:0 0 6px;font:13px/1.5 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2)}
  .rl-ends span{font:11px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}
  .rl-read{font:600 13px var(--sans);color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none}
  .rl-people{margin:0 0 6px;font:11px/1.3 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--ink-3)}
  .rl-tier{display:inline-block;width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;border:1.5px solid var(--lc,var(--accent));
    margin-right:7px;vertical-align:-1px;box-sizing:border-box}
  .rl-tier[data-tier="documented"]{background:var(--lc,var(--accent))}
  .rl-tier[data-tier="inferred"]{background:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent 50%,var(--lc,var(--accent)) 50%)}
  .rl-tier[data-tier="family-lore"]{border-style:dotted}
  .rl-ev{font:italic 12px var(--sans);color:var(--ink-3)}
  .rl-count{font:600 11px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--ink-3);text-transform:uppercase}
  .rl-nodes a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--rule-strong,var(--rule));text-underline-offset:3px}
  /* the people in a pen, and on a lane: listed, each a link, under the drawing at every width */
  .rivers-members{margin-top:16px;display:grid;gap:8px}
  .rivers-members .rm{border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:8px;background:var(--panel)}
  .rivers-members summary{cursor:pointer;padding:9px 14px;font:600 13px/1.4 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2)}
  .rivers-members summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:6px}
  .rivers-members ul{margin:0;padding:2px 14px 12px 32px;font:14px/1.6 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);
    columns:2 260px;column-gap:28px}
  .rivers-members li{break-inside:avoid}
  .rivers-members a{color:var(--accent)}
  .rm-why{color:var(--ink-3);font-size:12.5px}
  .rl-pen{margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px dotted var(--rule-strong,var(--rule))}
  .rl-pen ul{margin:6px 0 0;padding-left:18px;font:14px/1.6 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2)}
  .rl-note{margin:6px 0 0;font:italic 12.5px var(--sans);color:var(--ink-3)}
  @media (max-width:700px){
    .rivers svg,.rivers .riverread{display:none}
    .rivers-list{display:block}
  }
</style>
